cloister/rs/crates/sign/
========================

This crate (`leyline-sign`) provides CMS/PKCS#7 + X.509 + Ed25519
signing primitives. It was originally developed in the `ley-line`
project (https://github.com/agentic-research/ley-line, licensed under
Apache License 2.0) and lifted into cloister on 2026-05-09 per
cloister ADR-0007 + the cloister-side decision summarized in
ADR-0010 (vault precedent for cross-repo lifts).

**Upstream now public (2026-05-09)**: ll-open 0.2.0 lifted the same
crate from the (then-private) `ley-line` repo with the same
Apache → AGPL-3-or-later license bump. The canonical public location
is now `agentic-research/ley-line-open`, at `rs/ll-open/sign/`.
cloister's copy and ll-open's copy share an Apache-2.0 origin and
both relicense as AGPL-3-or-later; the two copies are kept in sync
by cloister-bd8c41 (NOTICE + targeted PRs upstream for cloister-only
additions like cert_chain.rs).

Per Apache License 2.0 §4(c), this NOTICE preserves attribution of
the work's origin. The Apache 2.0 license permitted this lift; the
original copy in ley-line (closed) and ll-open (public) remain under
their respective licenses. The cloister copy is governed by the
AGPL-3.0-or-later license in the cloister repo's LICENSE file.
Cloister contributions PR'd back to ll-open ship under the upstream
license terms (compatible — Apache-2.0 → AGPL-3 is one-way).

The proprietary parts of leyline-net that ley-line retains —
specifically the raptorq FEC layer and sqlite-blast — are NOT part
of this lift. cloister doesn't need them (per ADR-0005's amendment
section); the lifted scope is the open-spec crypto only.

