Cloister-side modifications since the lift (cloister-only, not in
ll-open's copy as of 0.2.0):

  - signingTime attribute omitted from CMS SignedAttributes per
    cloister ADR-0007 amendment 2026-05-08 (originally tracked as
    ley-line-e25413 before the lift). Reason: the wasm32 emit needs
    a per-host time source; a frozen placeholder shipping across
    hosts would silently collapse temporal binding. See `sign_data`
    doc-comment in src/cms.rs.

  - `lsign_alloc` / `lsign_free` exports in src/ffi.rs for wasm32
    linear memory management. Required for any wasm32 host (workerd,
    browsers, WASI) to pass byte buffers across the FFI boundary.

  - `cert_chain.rs` — new module. Verifies an ephemeral Signet cert
    is signed by the cluster master + extracts Interlace OID claims
    (epoch, peer_fp, scope at OID arc 1.3.6.1.4.1.99999.1.{4,5,6}).
    Used by cloister's lease middleware (cloister-bd7770).

  - `leyline_verify_cert_chain` FFI export wiring cert_chain.rs to
    the wasm32/native FFI surface. Returns claims as compact JSON
    (no serde_json dep — adds substantial wasm size for a flat struct).

These four pieces should be PR'd back to ll-open under
cloister-bd8c41 so a single canonical crate exists. Until then the
cloister copy is the source of truth for these specific surfaces.
